|caption=Logo of the Macaio Metro}}The '''Macaio Metro''' ([[W:Aragonese language|Aragonese]]: ''Metro de Macao''; [[Baliscano]]: ''{{lang|ca|Metro de Macayó}}'') is a network of elevated [[W:Rapid transit|rapid transit]] [[W:Electrified railway|electrified railway]] lines that serve [[Macaio]] and the city's [[W:Satellite city|satellites]]. It is made up of 8 lines. Two lines, [[Barcelona Metro line 9|L9]] and [[Barcelona Metro line 10|L10]], are being built at present, with both lines having different sections of each opened between 2009 and 2018. They are due to be fully completed in Q1 2024. Three lines on the network have opened as [[W:Automatic train operation|automatic train operation]]/[[W:Vehicular automation|driverless vehicle]] systems since 2009: Line 8 being converted to driverless first, and then Lines 9 and 10, opening up driverless.

The network length is {{convert|170|km|mi|0}}, with 183 stations, as of November 2021.
